ns to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only verified in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14955, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GcJshwxLc8X3cmcnucjfHC", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14955, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GcJshwxLc8X3cmcnucjfHC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18286, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Problem:** after the v2.3.1 deploy, the service was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. I skipped v2.3.1-rc because it had only been healthy in staging, never in production.\n- **Result:** all three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the current status. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before that version is deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YYifyefeHh2KDJDsDYfVZw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": 